{"created": "2024-05-06T12:41:39.980282+00:00", "modified": "2024-05-06T12:41:40.546001+00:00", "id": 10267550, "conceptrecid": "10267549", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10267550", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.10267549", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10267550", "metadata": {"title": "Data for: Caloric restriction extends lifespan in a clonal plant", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.10267550", "publication_date": "2024-05-06", "description": "<p>When subjected to dietary caloric restriction (CR), individual animals often outlive well-fed conspecifics. Here, we address whether CR also extends lifespan in plants. Whereas caloric intake in animals comes from ingestion, in plants it derives from photosynthesis. Thus, factors that reduce photosynthesis, such as reduced light intensity, can induce CR. In two lab experiments investigating the aquatic macrophyte <em>Lemna minor</em>, we tracked hundreds of individuals longitudinally, with light intensity \u2013 and hence, CR \u2013 manipulated using neutral-density filters. In both experiments, CR dramatically increased lifespan through a process of temporal scaling. Moreover, the magnitude of lifespan extension accorded with the assumptions that (a) light intensity positively relates to photosynthesis following Michaelis-Menten kinetics, and (b) photosynthesis negatively relates to lifespan via a power law. Our results emphasize that CR-mediated lifespan extension applies to autotrophs as well as heterotrophs, and suggest that variation in light intensity has quantitatively predictable effects on plant aging trajectories.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Chmilar, Suzanne", "affiliation": "University of Lethbridge", "orcid": "0000-0002-7003-5220"}, {"name": "Luzardo, Amanda", "affiliation": "University of Lethbridge"}, {"name": "Dutt, Priyanka", "affiliation": "University of Lethbridge"}, {"name": "Pawluk, Abbe", "affiliation": "University of Lethbridge"}, {"name": "Thwaites, Victoria", "affiliation": "University of Lethbridge"}, {"name": "Laird, Robert", "affiliation": "University of Lethbridge"}], "keywords": ["Aging", "Demography", "Duckweed", "Lemna", "Lemnaceae", "Lemnoideae", "light intensity", "longevity", "Photosynthetically active radiation (PAR)", "Senescence"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5061/dryad.4qrfj6qgz", "relation": "isSourceOf", "scheme": "doi"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "mit-license"}, "communities": [{"id": "dryad"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "10267549"}}]}, "notes": "<p>Funding provided by: Alberta Conservation Association<br>ROR ID: https://ror.org/030rn8443<br>Award Number: </p><p>Funding provided by: Natural Sciences and Engineering Research Council<br>ROR ID: https://ror.org/01h531d29<br>Award Number: RGPIN-2021-02967</p>"}, "title": "Data for: Caloric restriction extends lifespan in a clonal plant", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10267550", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/10267550", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/10267550?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10267550", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10267550", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.10267550", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10267550/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10267549", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/10267549", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10267549", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.10267549", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:10267550/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:10267550/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10267550/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10267550/media-files", "archive": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/10267550/files-archive", "arc